# AMBO — .gitignore
# Runtime entries are specified by SPEC-08 EB-081. T-004 verifies this file rather
# than authoring it from scratch.

# --- Environment / tooling ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
# Hypothesis example database (non-deterministic per-machine cache); ADR-007.
.hypothesis/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.env
.coverage

# --- Generated data (regenerable; see committed-by-design list below) ---
# EB-081 names these `data/warehouse/` and `data/cache/`; the `/*` form below is
# required so the directory itself is not excluded from git's tree walk, which is
# what lets the .gitkeep negation below actually track a placeholder inside it
# (a bare `dir/` pattern makes git skip the directory entirely — negating a path
# inside a fully-ignored directory is a no-op per gitignore(5)). Ignore coverage
# of the real generated contents is unchanged.
data/warehouse/*
data/cache/*
*.nc

# --- dbt ---
dbt/target/*
dbt/logs/
# dbt writes this on first invocation with a random per-machine anonymous-usage-stats
# UUID (`id:`) -- not reproducible, not meaningful to commit (plan 03-01 finding).
dbt/.user.yml

# --- Placeholders tracked inside otherwise-ignored directories (01-02 Task 3) ---
# These directories are ignored for their generated contents, but the directory itself
# must exist on a clean checkout for path-globbing scripts. Only the .gitkeep is exempt;
# the directories and their real contents remain ignored.
!data/warehouse/.gitkeep
!data/cache/.gitkeep
!dbt/target/.gitkeep

# --- Internal build scaffolding (not part of the published deliverable) ---
# The execution blueprint is process documentation for the build itself. It serves
# neither audience in Charter §1.2 and is kept local. The published specification is
# PROJECT_CHARTER.md + AGENTS.md + docs/ADR/ + docs/SPEC-01..09.
docs/EXECUTION_BLUEPRINT/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COMMITTED BY DESIGN — never add these (EB-081):
#   data/synthetic/           Layer P datasets + truth.json (the proof layer)
#   data/real_anon/           anonymized agency data (a€)
#   data/posteriors/*.parquet thinned posteriors, for report regeneration w/o sampling
#   exports/*.csv             DL-1 compares regenerated exports against these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
